    "catalog:tags": "basin, wash basin, accessible, wheelchair, wall-hung, bathroom",
    "catalog:note": "Accessible wall-hung basin with a shallow bowl set back behind a deep front rim, a lever tap. rim 0.72, bottom 0.59; the rim is clear under 0.67 for its front 0.11. The rim is one D-shaped outline sweep, 0.05 thick, less a circle outline sweep of radius 0.16 for the bowl opening; the bowl is a revolve whose outline, in true arcs centred on its axis, has its 0.012 wall, the waste hole the gap at its axis, filled by a metal waste. Trap below the bowl, waste arm to the wall.",
    "catalog:basedOn": "Approved Document M and BS 8300-2 via the drafting standard key dimensions: rim 0.72 (720 to 740 in secondary summaries; documents not read), clear under 0.67 unverified; 0.60 x 0.55 practice size and bowl, unverified. Port sizes from the drafting standard (BS EN 12056-2 conventions), unverified",
